# Bundled third-party plugins synced from the plugin marketplace by
# scripts/sync-bundled-plugins.mjs. They ship inside the installer via
# extraResources but are not versioned here: 100+ MiB of assets with their own
# release cadence, regenerable from the catalog. The two first-party plugins
# stay tracked, and so does the vendored `pi.prompt-enhancement` release, whose
# Composer action is part of the shipped product and must not depend on a
# marketplace download.
/apps/desktop/resources/plugins/*
!/apps/desktop/resources/plugins/pi.browser/
!/apps/desktop/resources/plugins/pi.file-manager/
!/apps/desktop/resources/plugins/pi.prompt-enhancement/
# Intranet distribution: these marketplace plugins ship inside the package and
# the build machine has no route to the plugin center, so they are tracked here
# instead of being re-synced by scripts/sync-bundled-plugins.mjs at build time.
!/apps/desktop/resources/plugins/pi.gitlens/
!/apps/desktop/resources/plugins/io.github.muzimu217.vision-kit/
!/apps/desktop/resources/plugins/pi.todo/
!/apps/desktop/resources/plugins/autotest/
!/apps/desktop/resources/plugins/pi.token-insights/
# Startup-resilience fixes ship inside these three plugins: each one broke the
# plugin restore chain at launch (a host API that does not exist, an
# undeclared bus permission with a colon-separated topic, a hard-coded data
# path). The fixes must survive the next marketplace sync, so the folders are
# tracked here the same way as the intranet plugins above.
!/apps/desktop/resources/plugins/pi.agents-anywhere/
!/apps/desktop/resources/plugins/io.github.xideadev.task-dida/
!/apps/desktop/resources/plugins/io.github.new-beginner.session-usage/
# The plugin host writes a `package.json` into a plugin folder that ships none,
# so Node resolves the plugin's submodules as CommonJS
# (`plugin-host-process.mjs`, `ensureCommonJsPackage`). The released
# `pi.prompt-enhancement` folder has no such file; the tracked copy stays
# exactly the released file set.
/apps/desktop/resources/plugins/pi.prompt-enhancement/package.json
# The plugin host writes a `package.json` into any tracked plugin folder that
# ships none, so Node resolves the plugin's submodules as CommonJS
# (`plugin-host-process.mjs`, `ensureCommonJsPackage`). Same generated file as
# `pi.prompt-enhancement` above, for the plugins tracked after that rule was
# written -- listed per folder because gitignore cannot express "untracked
# files under a tracked directory".
/apps/desktop/resources/plugins/pi.gitlens/package.json
/apps/desktop/resources/plugins/io.github.muzimu217.vision-kit/package.json
/apps/desktop/resources/plugins/pi.todo/package.json
/apps/desktop/resources/plugins/pi.token-insights/package.json
# The plugin host also writes one into any example plugin folder it loads.
/examples/plugins/*/package.json
/.plugin-packages/

# Python install artefacts
*.egg-info/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# The Python runtime this build ships: a full CPython tree plus the pinned
# wheel stack, regenerated on the build machine by
# scripts/bundle-python-runtime.mjs from scripts/python-runtime.lock.json.
# Hundreds of megabytes of third-party binaries with their own release cadence,
# exactly like the marketplace plugins above — versioned as a lock file, never
# as a tree.
/apps/desktop/resources/python/
/.python-staging/

# Local scratch work (audit scripts, throwaway output)
.scratch/

# E2E and fixture output that lands in the checkout rather than a scratch dir:
# the storage suites write .artifacts/ beside the repo root, the transcript
# history suite falls back to a repository-root temp directory when
# PI_SCRATCH_DIR is unset, and an Electron fallback-UI build leaves its own
# profile directory inside the app. None of it is product data.
/.artifacts/
/history-loading-*/
/apps/desktop/.fallback-ui-*/

# The plugin host writes a CommonJS marker package.json into every plugin
# folder it loads, not just the prompt-enhancement one above.
/apps/desktop/resources/plugins/*/package.json
